WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:10.000
In the middle of a global pandemic, a ragtag
group of welders, heavy machine operators

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.010
and builders were brought together.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:32.259
They were given plans for a mysterious structure.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:37.170
With little information on what exactly they
were building, their only clue was scrawled

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.989
across the top of their plans.

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:41.260
Spinlaunch.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.089
A space catapult.

00:00:45.089 --> 00:00:51.299
In this exclusive, behind the scenes documentary,
I talked to the people behind this new innovative

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:53.729
company.

00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:58.620
Spinlaunch is attempting to subvert a problem
that plagues the space industry, the rocket

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.510
equation.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:05.720
The rocket equation has been the tyrant engineers
have feuded with from the dawn of the space

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.720
age.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.730
A simple equation that describes how much
fuel a rocket needs to carry a payload to

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.360
its destination.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.280
The tyranny of this equation, is that the
fuel needed to deliver that payload is a payload

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.280
itself.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.010
A compounding problem that makes rockets more
fuel than rocket,

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.300
Typical rockets are more than 90% percent
fuel.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.990
Spinlaunch is trying to change that paradigm,
by imparting as much velocity as possible

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:37.960
to the payload on the ground, eliminating
as much fuel as possible from the rocket's

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:44.350
weight while greatly reducing the size and
complexity of non-reusable components.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.350
Their plan?

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:50.830
To spin a small rocket in a centrifugal mass
accelerator under vacuum up to an astonishing

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.120
speed before releasing it.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.740
Punching through the thickest layers of our
atmosphere at hypersonic speeds.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:03.950
Gaining 72 kilometers of altitude off nothing
but pure kinetic energy, before splitting

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:09.530
its fairings and unveiling a substantially
miniaturized 2 stage rocket to continue its

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:11.530
journey into orbit.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.629
You may question the numbers here, but this
isn’t the first time this has been done.

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:23.099
Project Harp, standing for high altitude research
project, managed to get a projectile to 180

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:27.239
kilometers of altitude with a high powered
gun.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:32.999
They achieved a muzzle velocity nearly identical
to Spinlaunch’s planned launch velocity.

00:02:32.999 --> 00:02:39.829
However, scaling a kinetic energy launch system
up, to launch a 10 tonne projectile needs

00:02:39.829 --> 00:02:41.420
spinlaunch’s technology.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.060
Ofcourse, all of this is easier said than
done.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.840
The challenge facing Spinlaunch’s engineers
is immense.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.780
This endeavor demands several new key enabling
technologies.

